{"author":{"id":"417295a7cc0952a9a38b67be3a894daed91f9069f7407e038d12a4f9b9a8451e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792346899,"nonce":"qBp0u31qbSTbMf6IAh+hkWmwSNo=","title":"RayScript view runtime: signals, templates and the op stream","message":"What exists (crates/rayscript-vm/src/view): signal/computed/effect/untrack/onCleanup/flush; markup compiled to templates (__el, __frag, __hole, __if, __for); mount/unmount; an op stream (ViewOp) with a checking host model (Dom); events in through Vm::view_dispatch; `rayscript view file.rays` prints the tree.\n\nDecisions\n- Markup builds data, not elements. Mounting builds nodes and gives each changing part (hole, attribute, spread, branch, list) its own effect. Components run at mount, in their own scope, so signals and cleanups made in them end with them.\n- Signals and computeds are heap objects (collected when unreachable); nodes are a table with explicit lifetimes, because the host holds the other half. Node ids are never reused.\n- Effects run on view_flush/view_pump, not at the write: one handler setting three signals is one round. Computeds are pulled when read. Dirty/Check marking, so a diamond runs once and a computed that comes out the same stops the update.\n- An effect runs once at creation (to find its reads). A function an effect returns is a cleanup. Everything created during a run is disposed before the next.\n- A signal where a value is shown (hole, attribute, list, condition) stands for its value and is read there. `$sig` in a string is not unwrapped: it would not be tracked.\n- Groups (fragment, hole, branch, list content) exist only in the runtime; the host never sees a marker node. Insert positions are worked out by looking past the end of a group.\n- \u003cfor\u003e matches items by value (identity for objects, content for strings), by value and key when the body takes two parameters. Unchanged start and end are skipped; the middle is matched by hash and moved by longest increasing run. A random-update test checks it against a fresh draw.\n- Events are `onClick` etc.; the event name is the rest with its first letter lowered (`click`, `mouseDown`). A handler runs as a fiber, so it may wait.\n- Mount gives the host an element tagged `#root` with a `name` property; the host puts it where the name says.\n\nTimings (release, one machine; `cargo test -p rayscript-vm --release --test view_bench -- --ignored --nocapture`)\n- mount 10,000 rows with two effects each: 44 ms\n- one hole changes with 10,000 rows present: 0.6 us\n- one of 10,000 items replaced: 1.1 ms (2.7 ms before skipping the unchanged start and end)\n- one signal sets a class on 10,000 rows: 39 ms, 200,000 ops\n- 10,000 rows reversed: 4.8 ms\n- 2,000 components with a signal each: 12 ms\n\nNot done\n- Host process and wire protocol for the ops and events (next).\n- Native FFI, hot reload, `ref`, context, error boundaries, a `class` utility resolver (host side).\n- Follow-ups filed separately: a fuel budget for calls made from effects; pooled fibers for calls from natives.","files":null}]}